    "objective": "Use maximum spacing to deny the press easy double-team angles on the ball handler.",
    "setup": "Five offensive players spread wide across the full width of the backcourt facing full-court pressure.",
    "organization": "",
    "instructions": [
      "The inbounder looks for the widest, most open outlet first.",
      "Receivers stay spread, resisting the urge to bunch toward the ball.",
      "Advance the ball quickly with simple, safe passes up the floor.",
      "Reset with a coach calling out which type of press (zone or man) to simulate."
    ],
    "coachingPoints": [
      "Keep real width between every pair of offensive players.",
      "Advance with purpose, not aimless sideways passing.",
      "Stay patient — spacing works, but only if nobody bunches up under pressure."
    ],
    "commonMistakes": [
      "Players drifting toward the ball out of nervousness, inviting a double-team.",
      "Rushing a risky pass instead of trusting the spacing to create a safe one.",
      "Panicking under pressure instead of looking for the simple, safe pass."
    ],
